# Codify AI - Project Diagrams

This document contains architectural and conceptual diagrams representing the structure and workflows of the Codify AI project.

## 1. System Architecture Diagram

This diagram illustrates the high-level decoupled architecture of the application, showing the interaction between the Streamlit frontend, the Groq Cloud AI engine, and the SQLite persistence layer.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Client Layer
        User([User])
    end

    subgraph Presentation Layer
        App[Streamlit Frontend<br/>app.py]
        Auth[Session Management]
        UI[UI Components & Forms]
    end

    subgraph Logic Layer
        Engine[Inference Engine]
        DatasetParser[Dataset Parser<br/>Pandas]
    end

    subgraph External APIs
        Groq((Groq Cloud API<br/>Llama-3.3-70B))
    end

    subgraph Data Layer
        DB[(SQLite DB<br/>codify_pro.db)]
    end

    User -->|Interacts| UI
    UI --> Auth
    Auth --> Engine
    UI -->|Uploads CSV/Excel| DatasetParser
    DatasetParser --> Engine
    Engine -->|LLM Prompt| Groq
    Groq -->|Generated Code| Engine
    Engine -->|Saves Query & Result| DB
    UI -.->|Reads Recent Logs| DB
```

## 2. Sequence Diagram (Code Synthesis Flow)

This sequence diagram details the chronological execution of interactions when a user generates AI code or analyzes a dataset.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant UI as Streamlit UI
    participant Session as Session State
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant API as Groq API

    User->>UI: Logs in (Credentials)
    UI->>Session: Set logged_in = True, booting = True
    UI-->>User: Display Boot HUD
    UI->>Session: Set booting = False
    
    User->>UI: Enter prompt / Upload dataset
    User->>UI: Click "Synthesize"
    UI->>UI: Display Loading Cube
    
    UI->>API: Send context + prompt
    Note over API: Inference via Llama-3.3-70B
    API-->>UI: Return Response (Code/Analysis)
    
    UI->>DB: INSERT INTO history (query, code, language)
    UI-->>User: Display System Output
```

## 3. Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagram

This represents the schema design of the local SQLite database used for auditing and session history.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    HISTORY {
        TEXT query "User prompt or dataset context details"
        TEXT code "The generated system output/code"
        TEXT language "Target language requested (e.g., Python, Excel)"
    }
```

## 4. Activity Diagram (User Navigation Flow)

This state diagram captures the user's navigational flowchart through the different states of the application.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> LoginPage: Application Loads
    
    LoginPage --> BootSequence: Enter Credentials & Sign In
    BootSequence --> NeuralGenerator: Boot HUD Completes
    
    state Menu_Navigation {
        NeuralGenerator --> TechManifesto: Click "Tech Manifesto"
        TechManifesto --> NeuralGenerator: Click "Neural Generator"
    }
    
    NeuralGenerator --> ProcessInput: Input Query / Upload Data
    ProcessInput --> AwaitInference: Click Synthesize
    AwaitInference --> DisplayResults: Response Received
    DisplayResults --> NeuralGenerator: Ready for next task
    
    Menu_Navigation --> [*]: Click "Terminate Session"
```

## 5. Data Flow Diagram (DFD - Level 1)

This Data Flow Diagram illustrates how information flows through the Codify AI system, including user inputs, external AI processing, and local data storage.

```mermaid
graph TD
    User([User])
    Auth((1. Authenticate<br/>Session))
    Input((2. Process<br/>Inputs))
    Generate((3. Synthesize<br/>Code))
    Storage((4. Store<br/>History))
    
    DB[(SQLite Database)]
    Llama([Groq Cloud API])

    User -->|Credentials| Auth
    Auth -->|Login Status| User
    
    User -->|Prompt / Dataset| Input
    Input -->|Context & Prompt| Generate
    
    Generate -->|Formatted Request| Llama
    Llama -->|Generated Code Response| Generate
    
    Generate -->|Synthesis Results| User
    Generate -->|Query & Code| Storage
    Storage -->|Record| DB
```
